{
  "id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/grainstone",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "grainstone",
    "es": "grainstone"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "Carbonate sedimentary rock with recognizable depositional fabric that is grain-supported, and constituent particles are of intrabasinal origin; contains little or no mud matrix. distinction from sandstone is based on interpretation of intrabasinal origin of clasts and grain-supported fabric, but grainstone definition does not include a grain size criteria.",
    "es": "Roca sedimentaria carbonatada con matriz original reconocible, grano-soportada, constituida fundamentalmente por aloquímicos y sin matriz micrítica. se diferencia de las areniscas por el carácter intracuencal de sus clastos y por su fábrica grano-soportada, pero la definición de grainstone no contempla el criterio del tamaño de grano."
  },
  "broader": {
    "id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sedimentaria-carbonatada",
